{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"A `:blocked` read cannot prove that the peer answered: the remote handle also returns it locally while waiting. Liveness therefore needs correlated response progress inside the stream layer. A healthy peer reporting “no new head” must stay connected; a silent channel may be retired without invalidating the installed head.\n"}}
