{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\np=Path('collab/1791304310868-architect-transport-mob-r2.prompt.md')\np.write_text('Created-GMT: '+datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT')+'\\\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\\\n# Task: Reconcile architect mob positions\\\\nRead the r1 brief and your r1 report. Read-only, no delegation, complete now. Astra accepts reject-at-cap ONLY with expiry/idle reap, existing explicit dispatch (no registry), finite contract, TCP now, name distinct from identity, interface enumeration as portable wildcard default with override. Optional route hint may refine a unique candidate but no mandatory network probe or universal NAT claim.\\\\n\\\\nPlease adjudicate these disagreements explicitly:\\\\n1. Owner explicitly requires neither REPL nor linker care about transport. Excluding yin.repl.serve/connect/host migration may be an interim commit, but cannot satisfy completed D1. Descriptor construction that chooses :ws/host or transport also cannot stay in yin portable code. Yin may parse principal and pass an opaque endpoint specification; stream host assembly parses/formats/selects concrete transport. Keep board-name and exposure table in yin; move generic glue below dao.stream. Agree or give invariant-compatible alternative?\\\\n2. Rate bound plus idle timeout is NOT a memory bound: malicious client keeps sending small valid requests but never reads answers, thus is never idle while outbound queue grows. Need finite host output queue accounting/backpressure or hard teardown at a conservative per-session cumulative byte quota (no completion signal required, though teardown must release buffers). Unsupported host must remain gated rather than advertise hard bounds. Do you accept an actual byte bound as lift gate, without mandating a specific host API?\\\\n3. give-up-after cannot reuse :asks as-is: count-ask\"'! resets asks at resend-after; budgeted drain! may leave answers unread; several observers can poll same link per tick. Prefer supervisor in dao.stream with explicit supplied now/deadline, no clock reads, or independent count of scheduled unanswered rounds, not arbitrary calls. Correlated per-request completion; server idle expires separately; valid blocked answers keep source alive; unrelated traffic cannot reset request deadline. No new core operation or closed? predicate.'\"\\\\n4. S0 contract; S1 admission/lifecycle bounds; S2 all nested loops incl drain\"'!, pending retries/chase and bytes; S3 boundary migration/liveness/stop both board and REPL; S4 address selection/IPv6/all-host tests then gate. Changes may land independently while loopback remains.'\"\\\\nState agree/disagree per item with reasons <=900 words. Do not claim all-party consensus yet.\\\\n')\ns=Path('collab/1791304310868-architect-transport-mob-r1.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log').read_text()\nPath('collab/1791304310868-architect-transport-mob-r1.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md').write_text(s)\nprint(str(p))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
